data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# QA Verification Report — Dispatch d002\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe Hello greeting app at `refs/campaign/orchestrator` was verified against `DESIGN.md`. All inspected requirements pass. The app builds, serves, and behaves as designed.\\n\\n## What was run\\n\\nRepository: `~/hello-app`  \\nChecked out commit: `1d41903e4f78f86db774829668949e0dac831186` (`refs/campaign/orchestrator`)\\n\\nCommands executed:\\n\\n1. `npm install` — dependencies installed successfully (0 vulnerabilities).\\n2. `npm run build` — Vite production build completed without errors.\\n3. `npm run serve` — Vite preview server started on `0.0.0.0:5173`.\\n4. `chromium-browser --headless --no-sandbox --disable-gpu --dump-dom http://localhost:5173/` — captured the hydrated DOM.\\n5. A Node + `puppeteer-core` script drove Chromium against the served app to inspect elements and click each colour button.\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n### Build and serve\\n\\n- `npm run build` produced `dist/index.html`, `dist/assets/index-*.css`, and `dist/assets/index-*.js`.\\n- `npm run serve` bound to `0.0.0.0:5173` and returned HTTP 200 for `/`.\\n- `vite.config.js` contains `server: { host: '0.0.0.0', port: 5173 }`, matching the design.\\n\\n### Interface against DESIGN.md\\n\\n| Requirement | Measurement | Result |\\n|-------------|-------------|--------|\\n| Header title is \\\"Hello\\\" | Hydrated DOM: `\u003cheader data-component=\\\"Header\\\"\u003e…\u003cspan\u003eHello\u003c/span\u003e…\u003c/header\u003e` | Pass |\\n| Footer text is \\\"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\\\" | Hydrated DOM: `\u003cfooter data-component=\\\"Footer\\\"\u003eBuilt with @codesweep-ai/ui\u003c/footer\u003e` | Pass |\\n| Greeting text is \\\"Hello, world!\\\" and is large/bold | DOM: `\u003ch1 style=\\\"color: var(--color-cat-2); font-size: var(--font-size-prose-h1); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);\\\"\u003eHello, world!\u003c/h1\u003e` | Pass |\\n| Default greeting colour is teal (`--color-cat-2`) | Computed inline style `color: var(--color-cat-2)` on first load | Pass |\\n| Four buttons present: Teal, Amber, Rose, Sky | DOM contains four `\u003cbutton data-component=\\\"Button\\\"\u003e` with those labels | Pass |\\n| Teal button changes colour to `--color-cat-2` | After click, `h1.style.color === 'var(--color-cat-2)'` | Pass |\\n| Amber button changes colour to `--color-cat-3` | After click, `h1.style.color === 'var(--color-cat-3)'` | Pass |\\n| Rose button changes colour to `--color-cat-4` | After click, `h1.style.color === 'var(--color-cat-4)'` | Pass |\\n| Sky button changes colour to `--color-cat-9` | After click, `h1.style.color === 'var(--color-cat-9)'` | Pass |\\n\\n### Design-system usage\\n\\n- `package.json` lists `\\\"@codesweep-ai/ui\\\": \\\"^0.3.0\\\"` under `dependencies`.\\n- `src/main.jsx` imports the required CSS files:\\n  - `@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/core.css`\\n  - `@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/app-shell.css`\\n  - `@codesweep-ai/ui/styles/components/button.css`\\n- `src/App.jsx` imports `AppShell`, `Header`, `Footer`, and `Button` from `@codesweep-ai/ui`.\\n- The hydrated DOM contains the package-rendered attributes:\\n  - `data-component=\\\"Header\\\"`\\n  - `data-component=\\\"Footer\\\"`\\n  - `data-component=\\\"Button\\\"` (on all four buttons)\\n- The greeting colour is applied via CSS custom properties (`var(--color-cat-2)`, etc.) and is updated through React `useState`, not by resolving hex values in JavaScript.\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThe app meets `DESIGN.md`. All requirements pass.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-report.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_37","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849624,"id":"chatcmpl-0ed189898872488bb9d48aaae891aded","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

